    {
      "id": "scene-03",
      "number": 3,
      "start": 39.875,
      "duration": 19.35,
      "audio_file": "scenes/scene_03.wav",
      "narration": "A tunnel is not much wider than the train. The gap around the body is narrow, and friction holds the air against the walls. To escape, that air must accelerate through a thin ring. The train pushes a volume equal to its own cross section, second after second. The air has no room to wait. It becomes a piston.",
