    {
      "id": "scene-04",
      "number": 4,
      "start": 59.225,
      "duration": 21.775,
      "audio_file": "scenes/scene_04.wav",
      "narration": "At three hundred kilometers per hour, the train covers eighty three meters every second. A tunnel ten meters wide holds thousands of cubic meters of air. The moving train displaces a river of it through a shrinking gap. Pressure rises ahead, falls behind, and the difference travels through the tunnel faster than the train itself. That is the first number to remember.",
