    {
      "id": "scene-05",
      "number": 5,
      "start": 81.0,
      "duration": 18.95,
      "audio_file": "scenes/scene_05.wav",
      "narration": "The pressure pulse does not stay smooth. It steepens as it runs, like a wave approaching a beach. In a long tunnel, it can reach several kilopascals. That sounds small, but a few kilopascals across a wall the size of a house is tons of force. The air is no longer a gas you can ignore. It is a load.",
