    {
      "id": "scene-19",
      "number": 19,
      "start": 358.985,
      "duration": 24.2,
      "audio_file": "scenes/scene_19.wav",
      "narration": "Eiji Nakatsu worked for West Japan Railway and spent his weekends watching birds. The kingfisher dives from a branch into water. It crosses the surface without a splash because its beak changes shape gradually. No sharp step. No sudden pressure rise. Water and air part around it with almost no disturbance. Nakatsu saw a pressure problem solved by evolution. The bird was not fast. It was smooth.",
