    {
      "id": "scene-20",
      "number": 20,
      "start": 383.185,
      "duration": 22.175,
      "audio_file": "scenes/scene_20.wav",
      "narration": "The beak became a nose. The team stretched the front of the train to about fifteen meters and shaped it so the cross section grows slowly. Air no longer meets a wall. It meets a gentle curve. The compression wave spreads over a longer distance, so its peak is lower. The same train, the same tunnel, a completely different pressure history. That is the difference between a shove and a squeeze.",
