    {
      "id": "scene-22",
      "number": 22,
      "start": 428.66,
      "duration": 22.25,
      "audio_file": "scenes/scene_22.wav",
      "narration": "The nose was not the whole fix. Portals gained hoods and vents that let pressure bleed away before it reached open air. Tunnels were widened. Track and train were tuned together. But the nose was the visible symbol of a new idea. Instead of forcing the air to obey, engineers gave it a path. That path came from a bird. Nature had already run the simulation for millions of years.",
